  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The denominators identify the decimal places: tenths, hundredths, thousandths, and ten-thousandths. Write each fraction as a decimal, then add matching places:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac1{10}+\\frac9{100}+\\frac9{1000}+\\frac7{10000}\n&=0.1+0.09+0.009+0.0007\\\\\n&=\\boxed{0.1997}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
